        "ja-Hrkt": "ライチュウ",
        "zh-Hans": "雷丘",
        "zh-Hant": "雷丘"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Raichu can store more than 100,000 volts, enough to knock out a Pokémon many times its size, and it uses its long tail as an earth wire, grounding the excess so it doesn't hurt itself. A fully charged Raichu glows faintly in the dark and turns grumpy, even with its Trainer. It's rarer than you'd think, partly because so many Trainers prefer how their partner looked as a Pikachu.",
        "guide": "The evolution of Pikachu with a Thunder Stone, a larger, orange mouse Pokémon that can store over 100,000 volts and grounds excess electricity through its tail. Raichu can Mega Evolve into Mega Raichu X or Y, and its Alolan form is an Electric and Psychic type that surfs on its tail.",
        "tagline": "Pikachu all grown up: 100,000 volts and a tail to ground them",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Raichu (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Raichu_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
